      "text": "Hi, how are you doing right now?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.44,
      "end": 16.2,
      "text": "I'm really sorry. That first stretch after losing a dog is so hard, especially with all the little routines that are suddenly gone."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 19.84,
      "end": 26.571,
      "text": "That's completely normal. Grief often shows up in those habits. It might help to still go for a short walk at that time, just for you."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 30.731,
      "end": 35.111,
      "text": "Kids often process grief that way. It's okay to say we'll think about it when we're ready."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 37.741,
      "end": 41.641,
      "text": "Good to question it. I still think it's right, though you know your situation best."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 49.521,
      "end": 57.181,
      "text": "Lots of people feel that. A new dog wouldn't replace him, it'd be its own relationship. There's no right timing, only what feels right for your family."
